```

## Real-board model selection

The previous 300 development wells have already been inspected in aggregate. For a stronger confirmation, extend the frozen role prefix with a new untouched `confirm` pool rather than pretending a split of the already-viewed board is pristine. The extractor assigns `confirm` last and can assert that every prior eval/cohort/dev well retains its role.

```powershell
python scripts/extract_real_board.py `
  --eval 1000 `
  --cohort 400 `
  --dev 300 `
  --confirm 150 `
  --out "board/private-v13" `
  --assert-role-prefix-from "board/private/wells.csv" `
  --production-chunk-size 25 `
  --statement-timeout-ms 300000
```

Both `board/private/` and `board/private-v13/` are gitignored. Use the original benchmark repository only as an independent control identity check.

```powershell
python scripts/run_v13_selection.py `
  --board "board/private-v13" `
  --legacy-src "C:\Users\jonat\Downloads\forecast-benchmark-main\forecast-benchmark-main\src" `
  --smartcast-src ".\src" `
  --boot 20000 `
  --out "board/results/v13-selection" `
  --report-only
```

The script:

1. uses only `role=dev` and disjoint `role=cohort` wells;
2. splits development wells deterministically within play × history bucket;
3. selects one pre-registered profile on the tune subset;
4. tests that choice once on the untouched confirmation subset;
5. checks exact parity between the packaged SciPy control and the historical repository;
6. fails promotion unless the confidence interval, effect-size, catastrophic-error, segment, and failure gates all pass.

Read:

```powershell
Get-Content board/results/v13-selection/deployment_profile.json
Get-Content board/results/v13-selection/selection.json
```

If no profile passes, the deployment recommendation remains `scipy_control`.

## Independent second confirmation

The first 150-well confirmation run favored `cohort_conservative` by roughly 14%, but its clustered 95% interval ended at `+0.0006`. That pool is now spent and must not be used for further selection or tuning.

Append a new `confirm2` pool while preserving every existing eval/cohort/dev/confirm assignment:

```powershell
python scripts/extract_real_board.py `
  --eval 1000 `
  --cohort 400 `
  --dev 300 `
  --confirm 150 `
  --confirm2 300 `
  --out "board/private-v131" `
  --assert-role-prefix-from "board/private-v13/wells.csv" `
  --wells-table "dde_remote.wells" `
  --production-table "dde_remote.production" `
  --production-chunk-size 25 `
  --statement-timeout-ms 300000
```

Then test only the already-selected profile. The runner cannot rank profiles:

```powershell
python scripts/run_fixed_profile_confirmation.py `
  --board "board/private-v131" `
  --legacy-src "C:\Users\jonat\Downloads\forecast-benchmark-main\forecast-benchmark-main\src" `
  --smartcast-src ".\src" `
  --profile cohort_conservative `
  --boot 30000 `
  --out "board/results/v131-confirm2" `
  --report-only
```

`confirm2` alone controls the promotion decision. Combining the first and second confirmation pools is permitted only as a descriptive robustness summary, not as a way to repeatedly test until a threshold passes.

## Bake-off workflow

### Normalize and validate

```bash
python scripts/prepare_spee_input.py \
  --monthly raw/monthly_production.csv \
  --headers raw/well_headers.csv \
  --out spee_data \
  --gap-policy nan \
  --duplicate-policy error

python scripts/validate_spee_input.py spee_data
```

### Strict Auto

Use the profile named by `deployment_profile.json`. Until a profile passes, use the default control:

```bash
python scripts/run_spee_strict_auto.py spee_data \
  --profile scipy_control \
  --horizon 360 \
  --forecast-start YYYY-MM-01
```

The selected profile and complete configuration are written into the run log.

### Vendor Best

```bash
python scripts/run_spee_vendor_best.py spee_data \
  --profile scipy_control \
  --horizon 360
```

Review the ranked diagnostics before applying any approved full-trajectory overrides. Strict Auto is never modified after its run begins.

## Profile board

| Profile | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `scipy_control` | Exact original SciPy bounded-Arps control; no added terminal rule |
| `anchor_only` | SciPy control plus 6% effective annual terminal tail |
| `candidate_gate` | Candidate curves may deviate only after a material inner-hindcast win |
| `recovery_conservative` | Limited endpoint-disruption recovery hypothesis |
| `cohort_conservative` | Play-specific, support-aware short-history shrinkage; no global fallback |
| `major_conservative` | Conservative candidate, recovery, and cohort stack for the major phase |
| `full_conservative` | Major profile plus secondary-phase ratio coupling; all-phase experiment only |
| `v12_fixed` | Claude v1.2 routing with the anchor and NaN defects corrected; diagnostic arm |

`v11_regression` and `candidates_only` remain research controls and are not offered as production profiles.

## Repository map

```text
src/forecast_benchmark/
  arps_scipy_v1.py   frozen original SciPy control
  arps.py            fast linearized and historical experimental arms
  smartcast.py       candidates, routing, recovery, cohorts, ratios, diagnostics
  profiles.py        pre-registered v1.3 configurations
scripts/
  extract_real_board.py
  score_real_board.py
  run_v13_selection.py
  run_spee_strict_auto.py
  run_spee_vendor_best.py
```

## Non-negotiable boundaries

- Never commit `board/private/` or licensed well-level outputs.
- Never tune against `role=eval`.
- Never drop failed forecasts from scoring.
- Never silently substitute a global cohort for missing target metadata.
- Never promote a profile on a point estimate alone.
- Do not claim SmartCast beats the control until the confirmation gates pass.
